# Codebase Patterns

## Project Structure
- React + TypeScript project
- Components in `src/components/` or `components/`
- Utilities in `src/utils/` or `utils/`
- Types in `src/types/` or alongside files
- Pages/routes in `src/pages/` or `app/` (depending on framework)

## React/TypeScript
- Use functional components with hooks
- Type all props with interfaces or types
- Use `useRef<Timeout | null>(null)` for timeouts/intervals
- Export components from index.ts when appropriate
- Use proper TypeScript types, avoid `any`

## Vega-Lite Integration
- Use `vega-embed` or `react-vega` for rendering
- Handle invalid specs gracefully (don't crash)
- Validate spec has `mark` and `encoding` before rendering
- Use hardcoded data: `[{region:'Almaty',revenue:120}, {region:'Astana',revenue:90}, {region:'Shymkent',revenue:70}]`

## File Handling
- Use HTML5 FileReader API for .jsonl files
- Parse .jsonl line by line (each line is JSON)
- Handle empty lines in .jsonl gracefully

## Streaming/SSE Emulation
- Use setTimeout/clearTimeout for delays
- Return cleanup functions for cancellation
- Accumulate text chunks in React state
- Handle incomplete JSON during streaming

## Error Handling
- Never let errors crash the application
- JSON.parse errors should return null, not throw
- Show user-friendly error messages
- Use try-catch blocks appropriately

## Testing
- Run typecheck before committing: `npm run typecheck`
- Verify UI at localhost:3000 (or configured port)
- Test with llm_stream_dump.jsonl file

## Git
- Commit format: `feat: [ID] - [Title]`
- One story per commit
